  "answer": "This has been requested before. Awake has no built-in schedule yet, so this is a feature request and nothing in your setup is broken. The maintainers track scheduling in PowerToys#24846 and PowerToys#27790 (duplicate requests, including #30227 for recurring weekday schedules, were closed in favour of those). A proposal there adds a daily start/end 'Scheduled' mode. It does not yet include weekday filters, which you would need for working days only. Add a 👍 or your use case to those issues. Until it ships, there are two workarounds. First, use Windows Task Scheduler to run PowerToys.Awake.exe with CLI options such as --expire-at=17:30:00 --display-on=false. The task can start at logon or on resume from sleep, or at a set time on weekdays. A PowerShell example is in #27790. Second, use a third-party tool such as Caffeine."
